issues.problem:
A hidden part can change who owns the overlap between two other hidden parts, and with it the mass, centre of mass and balance shown to the player. acrossTies places each part from the centre of the parts it ties with on volume, height and verdict (kept[q.index] == kept[p.index]), so a cleaned part ties with other cleaned parts. MassProps.ownership orders cleaned parts by that rank, after kept parts and slot rank. f7ac37d placed them from the world's planes, so no other part could reorder them.

Repro 1 (work/cs1.luau, cs3.luau): F2 with two 0.05 Dust Blocks in the Guard slot that overlap on the guard's front face, Iron at (0.2, 1.45, 0.12) and Steel at (0.23, 1.45, 0.12). Then add either a third 0.05 Dust Block buried in the guard at (0.35, 1.45, 0), which owns 3.5e-19, or a Ctrl+D copy of the Steel speck in place, which owns 0. Results on the tree:
- the specks' owned volumes swap: 1.125e-4 / 6.75e-5 becomes 6.75e-5 / 1.125e-4;
- mass 1.082753250 → 1.082752350 kg;
- balance −0.056912412870 → −0.056912460176;
- COM x 2.80992e-4 → 2.80814e-4;
- with 0.07 Dust Balls instead: mass −1.61e-6, balance −8.5e-8.

Repro 2 (cs2.luau): a blade section built as a sealed box of six 0.02 Blade walls round A (Iron) and B (Steel), each 0.25 × 0.55 × 0.075, at x ∓0.002. Both read Enclosed. Then add either A's solid buried in a solid Blade block at x 0.3 (owns 3.5e-18), or Ctrl+D B in place:
- mass 1.335547505 → 1.335344555 kg (−2.03e-4);
- balance 0.029996464 → 0.029940229 (−5.6e-5).

f7ac37d and round 1 read every one of these unchanged. Round 2 behaves as round 3. No G, factor or tier moves, because cleaned parts are in no work set.

SPEC statements this makes false:
- §4.4: cleaned parts 'never count for ... another part's place in either rank (the verdict's keys are each part's own, the measure's ties kept parts alone) ..., so a hidden part steers none of the physics a player is shown (balance, ...)';
- §4.5: 'a cleaned part counts for mass and COM by what it owns and steers nothing else, so no hidden part moves the balance';
- §4.3: '(... where it stands among the kept parts it ties with), so no id and no whole design's move decides';
- §17.2: 'No hidden part moves another part's place in either rank'.

No test covers how cleaned parts are ordered for ownership. A mutant that gives every cleaned part place 0 passes all 730 --quick cases.

