summary:
Round 3 fails on one major. The verdict now ranks exactly as at f7ac37d, apart from the height in RANK_Q. Hidden duplicates, near copies, mirror images, ids, moves along Y and Z (free, snapped, typed), turns and determinism all held. My own sample confirms it: 6,600 hidden-duplicate cases with 0 swaps; about 60,000 whole-design moves with no G change, kept flags changing only on X01/X01raw as stated; turns steadier than at M3; mirror differences only the named O11 (l) ones.

The major: the measure's rank still places cleaned parts from the centre of the other cleaned parts they tie with. MassProps decides who owns an overlap between cleaned parts by that rank. So a hidden part, such as a buried speck or a Ctrl+D duplicate in place, changes another hidden pair's owner, and with it the mass and balance shown: −9e-7 kg with specks on F2, −2.0e-4 kg and −5.6e-5 balance with near copies in a sealed cavity. No G moves. f7ac37d and round 1 do not do this, and SPEC §4.3, §4.4, §4.5 and §17.2 say it cannot happen.

The tried repair (var/fw) places cleaned parts from the world's planes, as the verdict does. It changes nothing as built on 11,486 designs and passes --quick (732 pass, 0 fail) with two new pins; one of them fails on the tree. Its only trade-off is f7ac37d's own, a Z move across z = 0 for cleaned near copies, which affects mass only.

Minors:
- three guard/place mutants survive on typed sub-1e-9 values; each has a tried pin that passes on the tree;
- T-PERF-01 fails a stretch under load on f7ac37d and the tree alike.

